own by about 1.3 percent so it'll be  interesting to see what happens  throughout the day because you saw a  significant decline precipitous decline  really right after the report came out  and then we kind of came back up and now  we've kind of come back down so  investors really trying to make up their  minds on how bearish is this for the  outlook for the stock market a really  interesting response you know I saw from  the bond market because bonds bond  yields really jumped up especially on  those longer dated yields 10 to 30 years  and then came right back down uh one  thing I want to talk about before I  forget  um the stock market has been on a tear  over the past two months the Dow  especially the Dow was up four percent  in November and up 20.4 percent in the  last two months that is the biggest  increase for the Dow Jones Industrial  Average since 1938. now the Dow is still  down by four percent year-to-date about  4.8 eight percent but with the strong  gains that we've been seeing on some of  this on some of the data and I'm going  to tell you about what data reports are  coming up over the next two weeks or so  that could again push this over we could  see the Dow go positive by the end of  the year which would be crazy given how  low we've been and especially crazy  given how low the NASDAQ still is the  NASDAQ was up 4.4 percent in November  but it's been down eight of the last 10  months it'll last 11 months excuse me  and is still down about 30 percent  year-to-date so the NASDAQ is down about  30 percent the Dow might end the year  positive that is a huge huge difference  and it's because those high-flying tech  companies are really just getting beaten  down by these fed interest rate hikes  the more it costs to borrow money the  more the market punishes those tech  companies that don't make a lot of  profit and even the ones that do because  again their their profits out into the  future are looking less Rosy when you've  got higher interest rates 